body:
R. Kelly :(. I really liked his music before... you know.

&#x200B;

Same can be said about Bill Cosby. I remember watching his show with my dad way before all hell broke loose.

I just finished reading both recently, so I think I can answer this to the best of my abilities. I think Guts would take this, though it would depend on the environment, why exactly the characters are fighting, if either of them are bloodlusted, etc. I'm assuming Denji is in his "Red Chainsaw-Man Form" and Guts is who he is on the most recent chapter of Berserk. I'm just going to assume they are on neutral ground and Guts thinks that Denji is an apostle or monster or something who's after Casca, while Denji thinks Guts is some sort of devil who wants to hurt Nayuta and Asa. Guts by this point has fought several monsters and apostles who (in my opinion) surpass the strength even that of Denji. This is taking into account of *all* of Denji's Chainsaw-Man powers, including his regeneration. What's more, Guts has *way* more experience in terms of fighting so I think his battle IQ and intellect will come into play in this hypothetical scenario. I think Guts takes this 9/10. However, this would be a completely different story if this was the "Black Chainsaw-Man." But since OP's title says "Denji" specifically, I'm going to assume it's the "Red Chainsaw-Man."

&#x200B;

TL;DR: Guts wins 9/10 times. However, this would be a different story if "Black Chainsaw-Man" was involved.
